The Ardia Linux host names the window class of the windows it opens for Little Ardia, Settings and Import
(g_ardia_linux_window_class: the Wayland app id and the X11 WM_CLASS instance, ardia-little, ardia-settings and
ardia-import), so a compositor rule and a desktop entry can tell them from a main window. It may also pin a window's
size (g_ardia_linux_pins_window_size): the browser widget's minimum and maximum size are then the window's own size,
so the window maps with a fixed size, which niri, sway and i3 float by default, and the host releases the pin once
the window has been presented. Both hooks are null outside the Linux host.
